\"lazy\"></figure>"],[16,127,0,"<p>Tighten the camshaft cap bolts to the specified\ntorque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>CAMSHAFT CAPS</p></td><td><p>M8</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Cylinder head side) 1.8 ÷ 2.0</p></td></tr></table></div><p>1. Fit the camshaft front oil seals (1a) using the tool (1b).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Fitting tool</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.948.000</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2015845.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[16,127,0,"<p>Fit the reaction rod mounting and fix it\nusing the nuts.</p><p>Fit the timing belt cover and fix it using\nthe bolts.</p><p>1. Fit the camshaft pullies.</p><p>2. Tighten the bolts (2a) for the camshaft pullies to torque using\nthe tool (2b) for counter-torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2a</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>TIMING GEAR DRIVEN PULLEYS</p></td><td><p>M10</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Camshaft side) 6.8 ÷ 8.4</p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2b</p></td><td><p>Counter-torque</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.822.146.000</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2015846.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[16,127,0,"<p>Fit the timing belt fixed tensioner and\nfix it using the bolt.</p><p>Fit the automatic timing belt tensioner\nand fix it using the bolts, without tightening them.</p><p>Remove the cylinder head from the support\ntools.</p><p>Remove the cylinder head support tools\nfrom the vice and return them.</p>"],[32,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Position the cylinder head (1a) in the vice, using  tools (1b),\n1 (c) and 1(d).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Mount</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.820.012.000</p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1c</p></td><td><p>Mount</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.820.050.000</p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1d</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.952.000</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2015847.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[32,127,0,"<p>1. Undo the nuts (1a) and remove the bracket on the engine for the\nreaction rod (1b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2015848.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[32,127,0,"<p>1. Undo the bolts (1a) and remove the camshaft caps (1b).</p><p>2. Remove the camshafts.</p><p>3. Remove the front camshaft oil seals.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2015849.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[32,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Place the camshafts back in their housings.</p><p>Place the camshaft caps back in their housings\nin the sequence shown in the diagram.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2015850.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[32,127,0,"<p>Tighten the camshaft cap bolts to the specified\ntorque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>CAMSHAFT CAPS/</p></td><td><p>M8</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Cylinder head side) 1.8 ÷ 2.0</p></td></tr></table></div><p>1. Fit the camshaft front oil seals (1a) using the tool (1b).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Fitting tool</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.948.000</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2015851.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[32,127,0,"<p>1. Fit the bracket on the engine for the reaction rod (1a) and fix\nit tightening the nuts (1b) to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Nut</p></td><td><p>REACTION LINK BRACKET ON ENGINE</p></td><td><p>M10</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Cylinder head side) 4.5 ÷ 5.5</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2015852.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[32,127,0,"<p>Remove the cylinder head from the support\ntools.</p>"]]